1
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:12,920
A reviewer tests 40 phones, and groups their battery life in hours into classes.

2
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:16,040
She has lost the individual results.

3
00:00:16,090 --> 00:00:18,060
Can she still find an average?

4
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:22,960
Pause the video and choose: yes, an estimate, or no.

5
00:00:23,010 --> 00:00:27,660
Yes, but only an estimate, because the exact values are lost.

6
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:35,910
Remember: the mean from a frequency table is the total of value times frequency, divided by the total frequency.

7
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:40,550
Use each class midpoint as an estimate of the values in that class.

8
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,870
Multiply each midpoint by its frequency.

9
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:44,540
Your turn.

10
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:46,820
Find the estimated mean, in hours.

11
00:00:46,870 --> 00:00:50,030
Pause the video and try it.

12
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:52,730
810 divided by 40 is 20.25 hours.

13
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:59,680
It is only an estimate, because we do not know the exact values in each class.

14
00:00:59,730 --> 00:01:04,090
The modal class is the class with the highest frequency.

15
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:04,960
Your turn.

16
00:01:05,010 --> 00:01:09,160
Which is the modal class: 15 to 20, or 20 to 25?

17
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:12,040
Pause and choose.

18
00:01:12,090 --> 00:01:15,830
15 to 20 hours, with 14 phones.

19
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:20,530
For the median, use running totals: 6, 20, 32, 40.

20
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:26,080
The 20th value is in 15 to 20, and the 21st is in 20 to 25.

21
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:29,070
So the median is about 20.

22
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:30,430
Here is the method.

23
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:33,340
Step 1: find each class midpoint.

24
00:01:33,390 --> 00:01:37,980
Step 2: multiply each midpoint by its frequency, and add.

25
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:41,310
Step 3: divide by the total frequency.

26
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:46,850
Step 4: find the modal class, and the median class from running totals.

27
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:50,640
Masses in kilograms: 0 to 10, 4 items.

28
00:01:50,690 --> 00:01:52,530
10 to 20, 10 items.

29
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:54,330
20 to 30, 6 items.

30
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:59,510
4 times 5, plus 10 times 15, plus 6 times 25 is 320.

31
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:04,850
Divide by 20: an estimated mean of 16 kilograms.

32
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:08,320
Brand A has an estimated mean of 20.25 hours.

33
00:02:08,370 --> 00:02:12,940
Brand B has 18.9 hours, but its results are closer together.

34
00:02:12,990 --> 00:02:14,940
A lasts longer on average.

35
00:02:14,990 --> 00:02:17,110
B is more consistent.

36
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:20,480
Max finds the estimated mean of the battery data.

37
00:02:20,530 --> 00:02:22,400
Which line is wrong?

38
00:02:22,450 --> 00:02:23,520
Line 1 is wrong.

39
00:02:23,570 --> 00:02:26,040
He divided by the number of classes.

40
00:02:26,090 --> 00:02:28,760
Divide by the number of phones.

41
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:33,240
810 divided by 40 is 20.25 hours.

42
00:02:33,290 --> 00:02:37,720
Census data, like ages and incomes, is often published in groups.

43
00:02:37,770 --> 00:02:41,580
Statisticians estimate the mean using midpoints.

44
00:02:41,630 --> 00:02:42,830
One last question.

45
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:49,860
Estimate the range of the battery data: the largest possible value minus the smallest possible value.

46
00:02:49,910 --> 00:02:53,140
Pause the video and answer.

47
00:02:53,190 --> 00:02:56,480
30 minus 10 is 20 hours.

48
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:59,760
To remember: use midpoints to estimate.

49
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:05,400
The estimated mean is the total of f times X, divided by the total frequency.

50
00:03:05,450 --> 00:03:08,830
The modal class has the highest frequency.

51
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:12,360
Find the median class from running totals.

52
00:03:12,410 --> 00:03:17,750
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.4 on Camday.
